{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  Pairing — food → bottle.

  Three axes, each option carrying a score per bottle code. Scores are summed
  and the leading bottle wins, with a running "trace" that shows the reasoning
  rather than just the answer. The reverse flow (bottle → recipe) is a separate
  section, pairing-recipes.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The design leads with a statement, and treats each question as a bold
  numbered heading. The port opened with an 11px eyebrow and replaced the
  numbered headings with a 'question 1 of 6' counter and progress dashes,
  which reads like a survey tool rather than a somm.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="non-pair-hero">
  <div>
    <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</div>
    <h1 class="non-pair-hero__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
  </div>
  {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
    <p class="non-pair-hero__lead">{{ section.settings.intro }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<div class="non-section" data-non-somm-root>
  <div class="non-pair" data-non-pair>
    <div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Filtered to axis blocks. This looped section.blocks unfiltered, so the
        three `reason` blocks rendered as questions 04, 05 and 06 — bare numbers
        with no question and no options, which is what was on the page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign axes = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'axis' -%}
      {%- for block in axes -%}
        <fieldset
          class="non-pair__axis"
          data-non-pair-axis="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <legend class="non-pair__q">
            <span class="non-pair__n">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
            <span>{{ block.settings.question }}</span>
          </legend>

          <div class="non-pair__opts">
            {%- assign options = block.settings.options | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
            {%- for option in options -%}
              {%- assign parts = option | strip | split: '|' -%}
              {%- if parts.size >= 2 -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="non-pair__opt"
                  data-non-pair-opt
                  data-scores="{{ parts[1] | strip | escape }}"
                  data-trace="{{ parts[2] | default: '' | strip | escape }}"
                  data-skip="{{ parts[3] | default: '' | strip | escape }}">
                  {{ parts[0] | strip }}
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        "Or just name the dish" — the design's free-text route, which the build
        never had at all. The three axes are a guided path for someone who wants
        to be led; this is for someone who already knows what they are cooking
        and does not want to answer three questions to say so. Losing it meant
        the page had no way to type a dish, which is the Somm's whole premise.

        Wired to the same somm.js the rest of the site uses: [data-non-somm] is
        what the script binds, and the seeds use [data-non-somm-seed], so this
        needs no new JS. Context 'pairing' so the Worker knows where it came
        from.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        THE VERDICT, ABOVE the free-text box rather than below it.

        It used to render underneath, so answering three questions pushed the
        answer off the bottom while the grey "or just name the dish" panel — the
        alternative route you had already declined by answering — kept the prime
        position. Now the recommendation appears in place and pushes the grey box
        down, which is what a result should do.

        The bottle and its add to cart live in here too, not under the
        photograph in the side column.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-pair__verdict" data-non-pair-result hidden>
        <div class="non-pair__verdictq" data-non-pair-title></div>
        <div class="non-pair__body" data-non-pair-body></div>

        <div
          class="non-pair__buy"
          data-non-pair-buy
          data-add-label="{{ section.settings.add_label | escape }}"
          hidden></div>

        <button type="button" class="non-btn non-btn--ghost non-pair__again" data-non-pair-reset>
          {{ section.settings.reset_label }}
        </button>
      </div>

      {%- assign dishes = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'dish' -%}
      {%- if section.settings.freetext_label != blank -%}
        <div class="non-pair__freetext">
          <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.freetext_label }}</div>

          <form class="non-somm" data-non-somm data-somm-context="pairing">
            <div class="non-somm__bar">
              <span class="non-somm__caret" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
              <label class="visually-hidden" for="pair-q-{{ section.id }}">
                {{ section.settings.freetext_placeholder }}
              </label>
              <input
                id="pair-q-{{ section.id }}"
                class="non-somm__input"
                type="search"
                autocomplete="off"
                data-non-somm-input
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.freetext_placeholder | escape }}">
              <button type="submit" class="non-somm__submit">
                {{ section.settings.freetext_cta }}
              </button>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The dish seeds sit INSIDE the form, as they do on the hero. They
              were outside it, and that one placement broke both things that
              looked wrong on the page.

              Every light-surface correction for the Somm is scoped
              `.non-somm .non-somm__seed` — because --non-somm-bg made the panel
              grey and the chips had to invert with it. A chip outside the form
              matches none of those rules, so it fell back to the near-black
              panel defaults: a #161614 pill with #b4b4b1 text, sitting on a
              near-black page. Unreadable, and not a colour bug — a scope bug.

              The squashing was the same mistake. `.non-somm__seeds` carries
              `padding: 0 18px 17px`, written to sit inside the panel, and the
              panel has `overflow: hidden`, so outside it the chips butted
              straight up under the bar with no gap and no alignment to it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if dishes.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="non-somm__seeds">
                {%- for block in dishes -%}
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="non-somm__seed"
                    data-non-somm-seed
                    {%- comment -%}
                      No data-answer. It used to be the dish label itself, which
                      made somm.js type the label back instead of asking — the
                      chips looked dead. Without it the seed falls through to a
                      real request, which is what naming a dish should do.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    {{ block.settings.label }}
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </form>

          {%- comment -%}
            Somewhere for the answer to land. This page had [data-non-somm-picks]
            in the verdict column but no [data-non-somm-stream] anywhere, so
            somm.js resolved `stream` to null — and pressing a dish chip ran
            straight into `stream.innerHTML = ''` in type(). It threw, and a
            thrown click looks exactly like a dead button.

            Outside .non-somm deliberately: the answer belongs on the page, not
            inside the grey panel, and the stream colour is scoped to the panel
            so text out here keeps the page's own ink.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="non-somm__answer" data-non-somm-answer hidden>
            <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.freetext_answer_label }}</div>
            <p class="non-somm__stream" data-non-somm-stream></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The verdict. The design pins a real photograph here with a live badge in
      the corner — this is the payoff for answering, and the port replaced it
      with grey placeholder text. The image is a setting so it can be swapped
      without a deploy, and it stays visible before an answer rather than
      leaving an empty column.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <aside class="non-verdict"{% if section.settings.somm_dot_colour != blank %} style="--non-somm-dot: {{ section.settings.somm_dot_colour }}"{% endif %}>
      <div class="non-verdict__head">
        <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.verdict_label }}</span>
        {%- if section.settings.show_live -%}
          <span class="non-verdict__live">
            <span class="non-sommbox__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {{ section.settings.live_label }}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        No photograph. The panel is the SOMM'S ANSWER, and a stock shot of the
        cellar said nothing about the bottle it had just picked — it was the
        largest thing in the column and the only part carrying no information.

        In its place the same living dash field the Contact page uses, drawn by
        contact-field.js on a canvas behind the picks. No envelope here, so
        envelope scale is 0 — that motif belongs to a contact form, not to a
        verdict.

        No trace panel either. It repeated the answered lines that the verdict
        column already lists, so the same three reasons appeared twice, either
        side of one result.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-verdict__stage">
        {%- if section.settings.show_field -%}
          <div
            class="non-contact-field non-verdict__field"
            data-non-contact-field
            data-density="{{ section.settings.field_density }}"
            data-ink="{{ section.settings.field_ink | default: '242,240,234' }}"
            data-envelope-x="0.5"
            data-envelope-scale="0"
            aria-hidden="true">
            <canvas></canvas>
          </div>
          <script src="{{ 'contact-field.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="non-somm__picks non-verdict__picks" data-non-somm-picks hidden></div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Something to say before a bottle has been chosen, so the panel does
          not open as an empty rectangle the way the header bands did.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="non-verdict__await" data-non-verdict-await>{{ section.settings.verdict_await }}</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%} Reasons keyed by bottle code, shown once a winner emerges. {%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" data-non-pair-reasons>
  {
    {%- comment -%}
      Filtered before the loop, not inside it. `unless forloop.last` was being
      evaluated against ALL blocks, so a trailing comma — and invalid JSON —
      appeared the moment a non-reason block sorted last. It worked only because
      r3 happened to be the final block in block_order.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign reasons = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'reason' -%}
    {%- for block in reasons -%}
      {{ block.settings.code | upcase | json }}: {{ block.settings.reason | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
</script>

<script type="application/json" data-non-catalogue>
  {
    {%- for p in collections.all.products limit: 40 -%}
      {%- capture c %}{% render 'non-code', product: p %}{% endcapture -%}
      {{ c | json }}: {
        "title": {{ p.title | json }},
        "url": {{ p.url | json }},
        "image": {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 200, format: 'webp' | json }},
        "price": {{ p.price | money | json }},
        "note": {{ p.metafields.custom.tastes | metafield_text | default: '' | json }},
        "variantId": {{ p.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }},
        "available": {{ p.available | json }}
      }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  somm.js, not just pairing.js.

  This section renders the full somm component — [data-non-somm] with an
  input and [data-non-somm-seed] dish chips — but only ever loaded pairing.js,
  which has no seed handling in it at all. The binder lives in somm.js:
  it initialises on [data-non-somm] and binds the chips. hero-somm.liquid and
  main-product.liquid both load it; this section was the one that did not, so
  the chips rendered, focused and did nothing on this page while working
  everywhere else. Nothing was wrong with the markup or with data-answer.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'somm.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'pairing.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Pairing tool",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "The pairing table"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "The verdict"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "verdict_label",
      "label": "Verdict label",
      "default": "The verdict"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "verdict_note",
      "label": "Verdict note",
      "default": "Three answers and I will commit to a bottle, a serving temperature and a reason. No hedging."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_live",
      "label": "Show the live badge",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "live_label",
      "label": "Live label",
      "default": "Somm live"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "somm_dot_colour",
      "label": "Live dot colour",
      "default": "#4ade80"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "What's on the table?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "Three questions. The somm shows its working rather than just naming a bottle."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "freetext_label",
      "label": "Label",
      "default": "Or just name the dish"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "freetext_placeholder",
      "label": "Placeholder",
      "default": "Whole snapper, charcoal, lemon"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "freetext_cta",
      "label": "Button",
      "default": "Pair it"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "freetext_answer_label",
      "label": "Answer label",
      "default": "The somm says"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "add_label",
      "label": "Add button",
      "default": "Add to cart"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "reset_label",
      "label": "Start again",
      "default": "Start again"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "verdict_await",
      "label": "Waiting line",
      "default": "Answer the questions and the somm shows its working."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Verdict background"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_field",
      "label": "Show the moving field",
      "default": true,
      "info": "The same living dash field as the Contact page, drawn behind the picks."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "field_density",
      "label": "Field density",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20,
      "info": "Lower is denser and costs more to draw."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "field_ink",
      "label": "Ink (R,G,B)",
      "default": "242,240,234",
      "info": "Comma-separated RGB, no rgb() wrapper."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "axis",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "question",
          "label": "Question"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "options",
          "label": "Options",
          "info": "One per line: Label | CODE:score,CODE:score | trace line. e.g. Starters | NON1:2,NON5:1 | Light plates, needs salinity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reason",
      "name": "Bottle reason",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "code",
          "label": "Bottle code",
          "info": "e.g. NON1"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "reason",
          "label": "Why this bottle wins"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "dish",
      "name": "Example dish",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Dish",
          "default": "Whole roast chicken"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Pairing tool"
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 30
}
{% endschema %}
